# What the daemon is sent as build context. Without this file the context is the working tree,
# which means `target/` (12 GB after a test run) and `frontend/node_modules/` — hundreds of
# megabytes uploaded on every build, and a context hash that changes whenever anything in them
# is touched, so no layer ever hits cache.
#
# Everything the image needs is listed in the Dockerfile: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, build.rs,
# src/, migrations/, shapes/ and frontend/. Nothing below is one of those.

# Build outputs — regenerated inside the image.
target/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Runtime state, never baked into an image.
data/
data-*/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.env
demo/.run/

# Not compiled into the binary: the shapes and vocabularies are `include_str!`d from shapes/
# and the migrations are `sqlx::migrate!`d from migrations/, but the rest is documentation,
# demos, deployment manifests and the test suite.
docs/
demo/
deploy/
tests/
compose*.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Makefile
README.md

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
